  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive a string `s` consisting of lowercase English letters.\n\nThe task is to find the **largest** difference `diff = freq(a1) - freq(a2)` between the frequency of characters `a1` and `a2` in the string such that:\n\n* `a1` has an **odd frequency** in the string.\n* `a2` has an **even frequency** in the string.\n\nOutput this **largest** difference.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** s = \"aaaaabbc\"\n\n**Output:** 3\n\n**Explanation:**\n\n* The character `'a'` has an **odd frequency** of `5`, and `'b'` has an **even frequency** of `2`.\n* The largest difference is `5 - 2 = 3`.\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** s = \"abcabcab\"\n\n**Output:** 1\n\n**Explanation:**\n\n* The character `'a'` has an **odd frequency** of `3`, and `'c'` has an **even frequency** of 2.\n* The largest difference is `3 - 2 = 1`.\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `3 <= s.length <= 100`\n* `s` consists only of lowercase English letters.\n* `s` includes no fewer than one character with an odd frequency and one with an even frequency.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
